# Candidate knowledge contribution for intel-oneapi-dpcpp 2026.0.0_220.
id:                     DRAFT-intel-oneapi-dpcpp-ohos-sycl-lit
status:                 candidate
trigger_tool:           llvm-lit|clang++|cmake|conan
phase:                  build|test
severity:               2
category:               llvm|sycl|lit|toolchain|ohos|cross-compilation
match_keywords:         SYCL_OHOS_INCLUDE, CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH, C_INCLUDE_PATH,
                        lit.site.cfg.py, config.environment, sycl/sycl.hpp,
                        algorithm file not found, libcxx-ohos, sysroot,
                        fsycl-device-only, FetchSource, FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR,
                        RTLD_DEEPBIND, dlinfo, Intel LLVM, DPC++
error_signature:        fatal error:.*(algorithm file not found|sycl/sycl\.hpp)|SYCL_OHOS_INCLUDE not set|lit\.site\.cfg\.py.*environment

root_cause: >
  DPC++/SYCL lit child processes are constructed from dict(config.environment).
  Supplying OHOS libc++ and sysroot paths through the parent process environment
  or lit extra_environment therefore does not reliably reach test commands after
  the site configuration is loaded. The compiler then sees its resource headers
  but not the OHOS C++ standard library, producing sycl/sycl.hpp errors such as
  fatal error: algorithm file not found. This is distinct from E075: the need
  is a narrowly scoped test-child environment, while global CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH
  remains unsafe for pkg-config-driven builds.

rec_approach:           scoped-lit-environment
rec_description: >
  Add an empty-by-default CMake cache variable SYCL_OHOS_INCLUDE. After the
  generated SYCL lit.site.cfg.py loads the main configuration, write that value
  to config.environment for CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH and C_INCLUDE_PATH. Pass the
  OHOS libcxx-ohos and sysroot include sequence only for the SYCL lit suite.
  Do not export it globally, and leave Linux/glibc behavior unchanged when the
  variable is empty.
rec_command: |
  cmake -DSYCL_OHOS_INCLUDE="<OHOS libc++ and sysroot include list>" ...
  llvm-lit -j1 --max-time=<limit> sycl/test/basic_tests
  llvm-lit -j1 --max-time=<limit> sycl/test/check_device_code
  clang++ -fsycl -fsycl-targets=spir64 -fsycl-device-only test_sycl.cpp

related_to:             E075, E217-draft-apache-arrow-cpp-test-ohos,
                        musl-glibc-full-comparison-iso-posix
deduplication: >
  E075 documents why a global CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH can make pkg-config discard
  cflags; this draft instead constrains the variable to lit test children.
  E217 documents generic CTest/GTest and FetchContent migration, but not
  generated lit site configuration or SYCL device compilation. The musl/glibc
  comparison records RTLD_DEEPBIND capability differences, but not the DPC++
  loader's source-level mitigation. The combined method is related, not a
  duplicate.

verified_on:            2026-08-06
verified_platform:      HarmonyOS PC aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos
verified_result: >
  A/B testing showed that compiler-only parent environment injection was not
  sufficient for lit, while setting config.environment after load_config made
  the value visible to child tests. The previous algorithm missing-header class
  was reduced from 51 occurrences to 0; reduction_range_deduction changed from
  FAIL to PASS; device compilation moved from 0/2 to 2/2 and group_algorithms
  from 0/1 to 1/1. Package consumer validation also passed clang++ --version
  and -fsycl-device-only.

limitations: >
  This does not make device runtime tests executable without Intel GPU, Level
  Zero driver, and OpenCL runtime. Remaining lit failures include expected
  diagnostic differences and target-registration/configuration limits. The UR
  dlinfo/RTLD_DI_LINKMAP review concern remains open and is not claimed as a
  completed portable capability-detection solution.

reusable_scope: >
  LLVM-derived projects on OHOS whose generated lit configuration copies
  config.environment into child commands, particularly SYCL or C++ tests that
  need SDK libc++ and target sysroot headers. The same evidence also shows how
  to separate scoped test-header injection, pre-seeded FetchContent source
  directories, and glibc-extension capability boundaries during a toolchain
  port.

evidence:
  - archives/i/intel-oneapi-dpcpp/2026.0.0_220/patches/sycl-lit-ohos-include.patch
  - archives/i/intel-oneapi-dpcpp/2026.0.0_220/conanfile.py
  - archives/i/intel-oneapi-dpcpp/2026.0.0_220/notes.md
  - PR #4458, commit 66b8a6c5bfb0ce396317147704b0f9d739d9832d
author:                 junshi_liu
